---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import muralPhoto from '../assets/photos/about-mural.jpg';
import relief from '../assets/photos/persepolis-relief.jpg';

const values = [
  {
    icon: 'target',
    title: 'Discipline',
    text: 'Nothing about his path was handed to him. Consistency, not luck, carried him from community college to leading engineering teams.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'compass',
    title: 'Identity',
    text: 'Knowing where he comes from keeps him grounded. His heritage is not a side note to his career. It is the foundation under it.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'users',
    title: 'Service',
    text: 'He builds for patients, workers, and communities, and measures his work by whether it makes their lives easier.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'book-open',
    title: 'Education',
    text: 'Education changed his life. He wants to open that same door for others as a mentor, educator, and community leader.',
  },
] as const;
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Sām Kazemi's story: from Antioch, California to Lead Software Engineer, and why he reclaimed his name and his Iranian heritage."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="An engineer shaped by where he comes from"
    lead="Lead Software Engineer, SFSU computer science graduate, and a proud Iranian-American committed to advancing his community through education, cultural awareness, and advocacy."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about">
      <aside class="about__aside reveal">
        <div class="name-card card">
          <Image
            src={muralPhoto}
            alt="Sām Kazemi in front of a Woman, Life, Freedom mural with Persian poetry and a red poppy"
            widths={[340, 680]}
            sizes="(min-width: 960px) 340px, calc(100vw - 32px)"
            class="name-card__photo"
          />
          <p class="name-card__op old-persian" lang="peo">{site.oldPersianName}</p>
          <p class="name-card__en">{site.name}</p>
          <p class="name-card__note">
            Pronounced “Saam,” not short for Samuel. Above, his name in Old Persian cuneiform, the
            script of the Achaemenid inscriptions at Persepolis and Bisotun.
          </p>
          <dl class="facts">
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="map-pin" size={16} /> Roots</dt>
              <dd>Antioch, California</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="graduation-cap" size={16} /> Education</dt>
              <dd>B.S. Computer Science, SFSU · Minor in Persian Studies</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="briefcase" size={16} /> Now</dt>
              <dd>Lead Software Engineer, MedManage Solutions · Lead Developer, Workforce Systems</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="languages" size={16} /> Languages</dt>
              <dd>English, Persian</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="heart-pulse" size={16} /> Outside work</dt>
              <dd>Weightlifting, fitness, martial arts, music</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="prose">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Where he comes from</h2>
          <p>
            Sām was born and raised in Antioch, California, to Iranian immigrant parents. There were
            stretches when his family struggled to make ends meet, and he lost an uncle he was close
            to. Those years showed him how much it takes to hold a family together.
          </p>
          <p>
            In the neighborhoods around him, he watched gang violence take a real toll on friends and
            on the wider community, close enough to see how quickly a life can narrow when the options
            run out. That experience taught him early that nobody was going to hand him a way out. He
            would have to build one.
          </p>
          <p>
            He decided education would be that way out. He started at Los Medanos College in
            Pittsburg, made the Honor Roll while completing his lower-division computer science
            coursework, and transferred to San Francisco State University. In August 2026 he
            graduated with a B.S. in
            Computer Science, a 3.53 GPA, Honor Roll and Dean’s List recognition, and a minor in Persian Studies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Why computer science</h2>
          <p>
            Sām didn’t grow up around engineers. What changed his direction was watching a close
            friend build a successful career in software. It showed him, up close, what the field
            could make possible: financial stability, real opportunity, and the chance to break the
            cycle of poverty for himself and his family. The more he learned about computing, the
            more he understood its reach, and he committed to it completely.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Why healthcare</h2>
          <p>
            Sām’s passion for health started in the gym. Years of weightlifting and fitness showed
            him how much strength and well-being shape a person’s life. While studying computer
            science, he discovered the other side of that passion: the enormous potential of
            technology in healthcare, and how new advances in computer science can help keep people
            healthy and even save lives. That realization drew him to the medical field.
          </p>
          <p>
            That passion turned into responsibility quickly. As Lead Software Engineer at
            MedManage Solutions, he architected <strong>ClearPath Virtual Health</strong> from the
            ground up: a HIPAA-compliant platform that helps care teams support patients living with
            chronic conditions. He leads its development, from scalable features and clinical
            workflows to a distributed engineering team. He is also Lead Developer at{' '}
            <strong>Workforce Systems</strong>, a startup building software for labor unions, where
            he designs the platform and helps secure contracts with the unions it serves.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Why Sām</h2>
          <p>
            Sām was born Mojtaba Kazemi. As he studied Iranian history, he learned where that name
            came from and came to understand it as a slave name, one imposed on his people rather
            than drawn from their own culture. He chose to reclaim a name that is theirs.
          </p>
          <blockquote>
            Sām is a name from Iran’s own epic tradition, carried by a hero of Ferdowsi’s{' '}
            <em>Shāhnāmeh</em>.
          </blockquote>
          <p>
            Sām (<span class="old-persian" lang="peo">{site.oldPersianFirst}</span>) is not a shortened Samuel. It is a
            Persian name with its own history, and carrying it is a daily reminder of who he is and
            who he answers to. “Mojtaba (Sām) Kazemi” still appears on some official records.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Heritage and community</h2>
          <p>
            His minor in Persian Studies was not a side interest. His long-term goal is to be an
            Iranocentric scholar, educator, and community leader: someone who helps Iranians,
            especially in the diaspora, know their history, language, and culture, and who advocates
            for them.
          </p>
          <figure class="relief">
            <Image
              src={relief}
              alt="Stone relief at Persepolis of Persian and Median nobles in procession, framed by bands of rosettes"
              widths={[680, 780]}
              sizes="(min-width: 960px) 680px, calc(100vw - 32px)"
            />
            <figcaption>
              Persian and Median nobles in procession at Persepolis, carved under the Achaemenid
              kings in the 6th–5th century BCE. The rosettes framing them are the motif used across
              this site.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <p>
            He brings the same discipline to that mission that he brings to engineering. As a mentor
            in the MESA Program at San Francisco State, he helped other students navigate academic
            and career decisions. He knows firsthand how much one person showing you what’s possible
            can change your trajectory. His aim is to be that person for others, and to build
            success that is grounded in identity and values.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Outside of work</h2>
          <p>
            Away from the keyboard, Sām’s biggest passions are weightlifting, fitness, martial arts,
            and music. Training keeps him disciplined and clear-headed, and it is where his interest
            in health began. Music is how he recharges.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head section-head--center reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What he stands on</p>
        <h2>The values behind the work</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        {
          values.map((v, i) => (
            <div class="card reveal" style={`--delay: ${i * 0.07}s`}>
              <span class="icon-badge">
                <Icon name={v.icon} />
              </span>
              <h3 class="value__title">{v.title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{v.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: 48px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: 340px 1fr;
      gap: 72px;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .about__aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: 104px;
    }
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .name-card {
    overflow: hidden;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--gold-bright);
  }

  .name-card :global(.name-card__photo) {
    display: block;
    width: calc(100% + 2 * clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px));
    max-width: none;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin: calc(-1 * clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px)) calc(-1 * clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px)) 20px;
  }

  .relief {
    margin: 28px 0;
  }

  .relief :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .relief figcaption {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .name-card__op {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--gold-strong);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .name-card__en {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .name-card__note {
    margin: 4px 0 20px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .facts dt {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-strong);
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .value__title {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
</style>
